$( <MM> <PROOF_ASST> THEOREM=tm2stkup3c  LOC_AFTER=?

* Four updates at three distinct indices, the outermost repeating the innermost, collapse to three: the update at ` I ` commutes inward past ` J ` and ` K ` (~ tm2stkupc twice) and absorbs the first (~ tm2stkup2 ).  Every iteration of the two-operand loops pushes on the output stack under the two operand updates and uses this.

